LiquidLaneAction
├── implementation configuration
│   ├── when the funding asset is zero
│   │   └── it reverts in the constructor
│   ├── when proxies share an implementation
│   │   └── they share immutable oracle bindings and keep independent budgets
│   └── when two assets have different fixed oracles
│       └── each oracle controls its asset's quote and swap ceiling
├── initialization
│   ├── when only a nonzero adapter is supplied
│   │   └── it binds the adapter and implementation funding asset
│   └── when the adapter is zero or extra configuration is supplied
│       └── it reverts atomically
├── asset authorization
│   ├── when oracle(token) is zero
│   │   └── quotes, swaps and budget configuration revert
│   ├── when a faulty override allows zero or the funding token
│   │   └── the base still rejects it
│   └── when an existing constructor oracle is bound
│       └── it prices and settles without creating an oracle proxy
├── migration
│   ├── when a new implementation is whitelisted
│   │   └── installed instances retain existing oracle bindings until migrated
│   ├── when the owner migrates to a compatible implementation
│   │   └── new oracle bindings take effect and active budget usage remains
│   ├── when the funding asset changes or migration data is supplied
│   │   └── it reverts and preserves the installed version
│   ├── when the old version used a registry
│   │   └── old oracle and allowlist storage cannot authorize omitted assets
│   ├── when the old version had no funding-asset slot
│   │   └── it derives the funding asset from the adapter vault
│   └── when an asset is removed and later readded
│       └── it cannot spend while removed and active usage survives readding
└── swaps and curator budgets
    ├── it preserves adapter-only authorization, funding units and period boundaries
    ├── it rejects unsupported assets, insufficient inventory and excessive prices
    ├── it rolls budget usage and token transfers back on failure
    └── it rejects reentrant budget changes and enforces budgets through Executor
